Nothing in these directions prevents an unvaccinated person from entering a site for:
(a) performing a law enforcement function that requires site access;
(b) fulfilling a statutory duty under Commonwealth law that requires site access;
(c) exercising rights under a Fair Work, Work Health and Safety, or Industrial Relations Act entry permit; or
(d) responding to an emergency when no vaccinated person is available.

Unvaccinated individuals may enter an airport or border crossing checkpoint to:
(a) perform a law enforcement function;
(b) fulfill a statutory duty under Commonwealth law;
(c) exercise rights under a Fair Work, Work Health and Safety, or Industrial Relations Act entry permit; or
(d) respond to an emergency when no vaccinated person is available.

Unvaccinated individuals may enter an airport or border crossing checkpoint to:
(a) perform a law enforcement function;
(b) fulfill a statutory duty under Commonwealth law;
(c) exercise rights under a Fair Work, Work Health and Safety, or Industrial Relations Act entry permit; or
(d) respond to an emergency when no vaccinated person is available.

Unvaccinated individuals may enter a community care services facility or accommodation to:
(a) perform a law enforcement function;
(b) fulfill a statutory duty under Commonwealth law;
(c) exercise rights under a Fair Work, Work Health and Safety, or Industrial Relations Act entry permit; or
(d) respond to an emergency when no vaccinated person is available.

Unvaccinated remote Aboriginal community workers may enter or remain in a remote Aboriginal community for:
(a) performing a law enforcement function;
(b) family or cultural purposes, for as long as necessary;
(c) transiting through, without contact with residents and taking the most direct route;
(d) residing in the community without leaving;
(e) fulfilling a statutory duty under Commonwealth law;
(f) exercising rights under a Fair Work, Work Health and Safety, or Industrial Relations Act entry permit;
(g) responding to an emergency when no vaccinated person is available; or
(h) any circumstance approved in writing by the Chief Health Officer.

